From 00c9190a2c6437b459be748bbc0ad56871e1fa17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sanjay Singh <sanjay@namsconsulting.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:23:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show the answer without a button press, on 76 calculators
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

110 of 117 calculators kept their result hidden until you pressed
Calculate — even when the inputs were already filled in. The FD page
opened with 100000 / 7.2% / 5 years sitting there and an empty result
panel beside it. That is one click between a visitor and the only thing
they came for, on nearly every page of the site.

This wires the existing calculate() into a useEffect on its own inputs,
so the result appears immediately and follows what you type. No formula
is touched anywhere: the same function that ran on the button press now
also runs as you type, and the button still works.

Two things fall out of that:

- The alert() popups inside those functions had to go. An alert on every
  keystroke would be unusable, and it was a poor way to say "that number
  is not valid" anyway — the result panel simply stays empty now.
- 56 files opened with empty inputs, so there was nothing to show. Each
  now starts from the example value the author had already written into
  the field's placeholder, which means the page opens on a worked
  example rather than a blank form.

Left alone deliberately: 9 calculators with several independent modes,
where recomputing one mode would overwrite the mode the visitor picked,
and files whose validation could not be made silent mechanically. Those
are hand work, in a later patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PHRT6vhhyEyck1uNY7XC3G
